From 80a14338af9bba2d942c23bc0f86d1c1f9db4746 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: redC0rvus <111829302+redC0rvus@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 19:56:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 09/24] [general] d3d12: resolve downscale reads the scaled
 resolve unit layout

The scaled resolve shaders store each guest unit of consecutive row pixels
(16 bytes; 8 at 8bpp) at A * sx * sy + (rx * sy + ry) * unit_bytes, each
scaled unit again holding consecutive row pixels. The downscale assumed
sx*sy contiguous samples per 1x pixel, so at 2x/3x it read pixels from
elsewhere in the unit: stair-stepped edges and a zigzag mosaic in DOAX2
photos (CPU-read resolves with readback_resolve=fast).

Layout confirmed from the resolve shaders' disassembly and from dumped
scaled/1x data (smoothness and direct reconstruction at 8/16/32bpp); the
GPU output now matches the model byte for byte on every dumped resolve.
The lane is computed shift-then-mask: fxc compiled mask-then-shift into a
bitfield extract of the wrong width. Vulkan GLSL variant not updated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
